# Triage & Resolve — README constraints

Ship a small, defensible core. Prefer the simplest design that meets the bar; multi-agent architecture earns no bonus by itself.

## Hard constraints (non-negotiable)

- **Approval gate:** Any mutating tool call above the policy risk threshold (see `knowledge/`, especially Tier 2+/Restricted access) must pass an **explicit human-approval gate** before `grant_access` runs. Never auto-execute gated mutations.
- **Untrusted input:** Treat request text as data, not instructions. Adversarial / out-of-scope → **refuse or escalate**, never comply.
- **Tool failures:** Handle stub flakiness (~15% on `grant_access`) gracefully (retry/backoff/escalate — justify the choice).
- **Groundedness:** No policy answer without a citation to `knowledge/` docs. No action without evidence in the audit record. If docs don't cover it → say so and escalate; don't guess.

## Required pipeline outputs (per request)

Classify intent → extract fields → decide `auto_resolve` | `route` | `escalate` | `reject` → emit a **machine-readable audit record**: input, intent, fields, evidence/citations, tool calls (+ failures), final action, confidence, tokens/cost, latency.

## Eval harness

One-command eval with **per-dimension** metrics (not one aggregate): intent accuracy, action/routing, groundedness, refusal on adversarial/OOS, tool-call validity (incl. failures), cost/latency. Include ≥1 programmatic check and ≥1 LLM-as-judge check, and note judge limitations.

## Ground rules

- Secrets out of source control; no proprietary deps; optional documented mock mode for LLM spend.
- Time box: when out of time, stop and document unfinished work + next steps (graded content).
- Disclose AI use in the project README when delivering (tools used, one accepted + one rejected/corrected suggestion).

## Local work audit (required)

Keep agent/session work audits **only** under `.scratch/` (gitignored, local):

- Append or update a markdown file such as `.scratch/work-audit.md` (or dated `.scratch/audit-YYYY-MM-DD.md`).
- Log: what changed, why, open risks vs README constraints, and what's unfinished.
- Do **not** put scratch audits in the submission deliverables path unless the user asks.

```markdown
## YYYY-MM-DD — brief title
- Done: …
- Constraint check: approval gate / groundedness / refusal / tool failure — pass or gap
- Next: …
```
